 "claims": [
  {
   "id": "K_hook",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "On 8 August 2026 customs at Haneda Airport, Tokyo, found about 200 lizards packed into 22 pairs of socks in the suitcase of a 23-year-old Mexican traveller arriving from South Korea. Narration: 'Customs checked his socks. 200 lizards.' / 'Stuffed in 22 pairs.' Headline '200 LIZARDS / IN 22 PAIRS OF SOCKS'.",
   "sources": [
    "fox",
    "gulf",
    "kyodo"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_delhi",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Customs searched Emirates flight EK-514 from Dubai after it landed at Indira Gandhi International Airport, Delhi, on 21 September 2026 (reported 14 October 2026). Narration: 'In Delhi, ...' (the line below).",
   "sources": [
    "national",
    "jurishour"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_paint",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The gold, in the form of chains, had been sprayed with silver and black paint. Narration: 'In Delhi, gold chains, painted silver and black.'",
   "sources": [
    "national",
    "jurishour"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_seats",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The painted chains, about 6.5 kg of gold (about Dh3.8 million / Rs 9 crore), were hidden beneath two seats, packed in three small bags. Narration: 'Hidden beneath two seats. Eight passengers arrested.' Label '6.5 KG OF GOLD'.",
   "sources": [
    "national",
    "jurishour"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_eight",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Eight passengers from the flight, including a woman, were arrested (accused only; never named or drawn). Narration: '... Eight passengers arrested.'",
   "sources": [
    "national",
    "jurishour"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_kenya",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Editorial rehook 'But that was not the strangest bag.' introducing: on 10 March 2026 a Chinese national was arrested at Jomo Kenyatta International Airport, Nairobi, trying to leave Kenya with live ants in his luggage.",
   "sources": [
    "reuters",
    "eastafrican",
    "timeslive"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_ants",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "About 2,238 live garden ants were found (more than 2,000). Narration: 'In Kenya, over 2,000 ants.'",
   "sources": [
    "reuters",
    "eastafrican",
    "timeslive"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_tubes",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "1,948 of the ants were packed in test tubes and the rest in three rolls of tissue paper. Narration: 'In test tubes and tissue paper.'",
   "sources": [
    "reuters",
    "eastafrican"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_year",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "He pleaded guilty and a Nairobi court sentenced him in April 2026 to one year in prison and a fine (about $7,700), with deportation afterwards. Narration: 'He got a year in prison.'",
   "sources": [
    "arabnews",
    "standard",
    "reuters"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_tokyo",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "At Haneda, customs officers noticed unnatural bulges inside packed T-shirts in the traveller's suitcase during the baggage check (police had passed on a tip-off). Narration: 'Then Tokyo. His T-shirts had bulges.'",
   "sources": [
    "gulf",
    "kyodo",
    "dexerto"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_inside",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Inside the T-shirts were socks, and inside the socks the lizards (2 to 24 per sock, Kyodo). Narration: 'Inside? Socks. Inside the socks? Lizards.'",
   "sources": [
    "gulf",
    "kyodo",
    "fox"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_count",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "STATISTIC: about 200 lizards in 22 pairs of socks; at least nine were preliminarily identified as Mexican alligator lizards (Abronia graminea), an endangered, CITES-listed species. Narration: 'About 200. Some endangered.' Counter '200 LIZARDS'.",
   "sources": [
    "fox",
    "gulf",
    "kyodo"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_price",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "FUN FACT: he told police he paid about 560-750 yen (about $3.50-5) per lizard in Mexico; some species sell for about 100,000 yen (about $640) each in Japan. Narration: 'Cost? Under five dollars each.' Card 'PAID UNDER $5 EACH / WORTH UP TO ~$640'.",
   "sources": [
    "kyodo",
    "gulf"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_punch",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "He was arrested on suspicion of violating the Customs Act (attempted unauthorised import) and reportedly admitted the allegation; accused only, no verdict found as of 18 Oct 2026. Narration: 'He was arrested. 44 socks, and not one foot.' (22 pairs = 44 socks: editorial arithmetic joke.)",
   "sources": [
    "kyodo",
    "gulf",
    "fox"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_part2",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "PART 2 TEASE (end card): June 2026, Mumbai airport: customs arrested a passenger from Bangkok with 29 live exotic animals, including a gibbon, in boxes in his bags; the animals were rescued. End card 'PART 2: A GIBBON IN HIS BAGS'.",
   "sources": [
    "uni",
    "navbharat"
   ]
  }
 ],
